by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-05-13T16:04:58Z","updated_at":"2025-12-22T19:45:09Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nreproducible in 4.4 (07e41850ef6c7c8bb7b35a39b080600b77e6953a)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (4d7c448a0) - macOS Sequoia (15.3.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Pro (Apple7) - Apple M1 Pro (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nEven when `_setup_local_to_scene` is implemented and the resource is set to local to scene, if the scene is instantiated the `_setup_local_to_scene` is not called.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a class inheriting `ViewportTexture`\n- implement the `_setup_local_to_scene` with a print\n- create a scene and export a variable of the class you created \n- set a resource to the variable you created \n- run the scene \n- see there is no print\n\nwith the MRP you can just directly run the scene there is two resource one inheriting resource one inheriting ViewportTexture. Both have a printbut  when running only the resource inheriting one will print.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20191614/mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106360/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106360/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}